WEBVTT

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.020
Finished so soon, my son?

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.630
Why no, you sent one.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.740
There must be some mistakes. I did not send for you.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:50.590
It was no mistake.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.560
My son!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.040
Don't know, but he seems to feel there is something amiss.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.770
I've not seen him since his friend Rama took him to visit the land of Tang Ho.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.210
Well, someone's taken him out through that underground passage.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.410
Impossible. Nothing like that could happen this month.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.750
Well, it did happen.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.400
All right.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.410
What even repel you?

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:08.430
What have they done with AIDS?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:10.680
Don't know.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.840
I was engrossed in translating the diary,

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:29.700
but suddenly I lost a page out of Traynor's diary.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.320
Do you know what was on it?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.370
Something about it.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:34.640
How can you...

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.840
Just saw the point of learning this back location when I was overcome.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.580
Now, gee, that's what the dragon's after.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.590
Anything I can do, holy one?

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.080
Help me to get Shang-Ho out into the corridor.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.920
I told you never to leave with your right.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.840
Am I glad to see you.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.620
The dragon has you.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.220
Exactly what I want people to think.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:26.900
I don't get you.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.180
I've got to find the missing page of Trainer's Diary.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.620
Go back to the plane and pretend you've got motor trouble.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:33.980
And they need you in a hurry.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.250
Go on, get away.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.780
Go on, get out of here.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.000
Go on.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.050
There you go.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.870
Go on, then buy yourself some candy.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:17.320
Hi, child. Hello, bye, child.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:21.890
Bye, child.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.230
No, sorry. He's not here.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:34.670
For you, Billy.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:39.880
Excuse me.

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:41.730
Not knowing you're still here.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.370
Jerry wants to talk to you.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.540
Jerry, one moment please.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.820
Go ahead, this is it.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.680
Sure, I'll help Ace, but he's right here with me now.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:06.690
Okay, tell Ace Happy Landing.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:07.690
So long.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:13.560
Baby, Ace is disguised as a native, and he's tracking down one of the dragons.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:16.260
To find out why the dragons are holding my father's with me.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:17.720
Jerry didn't say it.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.310
Bet you that's what Ace is having.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.500
Come on, let's go tell my dad.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:25.620
Go happy, please.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.740
Good afternoon, Miss Trainor. Have they found your father yet?

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.880
No, I can't live to keep it. But we hope to have him soon.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:40.410
I think you hope so.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.220
You nudged me.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.300
Don't you know a suspect he's agon?

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:58.000
Are you sure? I heard it with my own ear. We must send a message at once.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.110
Keep away from the hideout.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:11.830
No attack.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:13.820
Contact the dragon in person.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:16.940
The top is on your trail.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:18.900
The dragon commands.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.270
When do we eat, eh?

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.460
No, I always did like pigeon pie.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.560
You're not eating these birds, Jerry. They're carrier fishes.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:45.910
Carrier fishes?

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.410
Oh, hey, what are they carrying?

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:51.510
They're going to carry us straight to the dragon's hideout.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.490
Say, what means you think these birds know where they're dragons?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:58.190
I just saw one of their little pals turn loose with a message tied to his leg.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.970
Unless I'm mistaken, he's headed for the dragon's hideout.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.340
Right up.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:01.150
Get in.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.370
It's a page from Painter's diary.

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.620
It must go where the mountain of Jade is located.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.590
I've been waiting a long time for this.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.000
What are you going to do?

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.970
Now that we have that, Dragon won't need it.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:45.480
trainer.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.120
No,

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:52.820
we can start looking for the mountain of J's.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.750
What's the matter?

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:55.310
Can't you read it?

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:58.750
It's called a secret writing.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:03.280
Hey, Sargey! Wait, don't shoot!

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.340
What's the idea? We don't need him anymore.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:07.610
That's pretty cool.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.490
The diary tells where the mountain of jade is.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.330
Yeah, but it's written in some secret language.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.810
Well, he wrote it to make him read it.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.020
What sort of language is this, Praner?

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.520
Just what he said it was?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.730
Secret language. Only a few scholars in the world can read it.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:27.470
And you're one of them. Get busy and read it or...

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:29.530
Right.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.580
The government has discovered the secret.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.140
Meet me at the other end of the tunnel.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.230
You stay here and guard the prisoner and see that no harm comes.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:33.250
What are they?

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:34.180
Nothing.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:40.540
I just wondered what you would do if the dragon wanted to send the message for a picture.

00:16:30.124 --> 00:16:30.404
I've been around.

00:16:32.268 --> 00:16:34.528
Well, if they are, they're sure keeping themselves well again.

00:16:34.728 --> 00:16:36.428
Say, let's go up on that ridge and take a look around.

00:17:38.796 --> 00:17:39.476
one of our men.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:41.740
We might need it.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.220
You're the wrong man.

00:17:51.212 --> 00:17:52.552
those switches, see what you can find.

00:17:58.124 --> 00:17:59.184
It leads to their hideout.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:28.450
It's like a storeroom.

00:18:28.990 --> 00:18:29.870
We must be getting closer.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.680
to their hideout.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.710
The guy we tied up.

00:19:02.076 --> 00:19:02.916
Well, more ammunition.

00:19:03.452 --> 00:19:04.012
What are they?
